Build a polished, modern, fully interactive web application prototype called **“Public Grievance Tracker”** for a college hackathon.

This is NOT a simple landing page or static UI mockup. Build it as a functional website prototype with realistic navigation, forms, dashboards, case workflows, role-based views, seeded demo data, status changes, deadlines, escalation, resolution, and audit history.

The application should look and behave like a professional government/public-service grievance management platform while still having a modern, clean SaaS-style interface.

==================================================
1. PROJECT OBJECTIVE
==================================================

The purpose of the application is to make public grievances:

- visible
- owned
- trackable
- deadline-driven
- accountable
- resolvable

The central concept is:

A citizen submits a grievance → the system generates a unique case ID → the grievance is routed to the appropriate department/officer → staff manage its lifecycle → deadlines are monitored → overdue cases can be escalated → staff resolve the case with a resolution note → the complete history remains available.

The prototype must demonstrate this complete lifecycle clearly.

